---
title: Control
description: Associates a Label with a form control and hands the input a spreadable props object with every required id, name and ARIA attribute already set.
---

<script>
	import LiveFieldDemo from "$lib/demos/live-field-demo.svelte";
</script>

`Control` sits between a [Field](/docs/components/field) and the actual input element. It resolves the control's `id`, looks up the field's name, errors and constraints from context, and exposes a `props` object that you spread onto the form control. That spread is the whole contract: it carries labelling, description and error wiring so you never hand-write `aria-*` attributes.

It renders no element of its own.

## Live example

`Control` hands the input its `id`, `name` and ARIA attributes. Submit the form empty, then inspect the input: every one of those attributes comes from the spread, not from the markup.

<LiveFieldDemo />

## Minimal example

```svelte title="src/routes/settings/settings-form.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { untrack } from "svelte";
	import { superForm, type SuperValidated } from "sveltekit-superforms";
	import { Control, Field, Label } from "@emmorts/formsnap";
	import type { SettingsData } from "./schema.js";

	let { validated }: { validated: SuperValidated<SettingsData> } = $props();

	const form = superForm(untrack(() => validated));
	const { form: formData } = form;
</script>

<Field {form} name="email" fieldErrors>
	<Control id="email-input">
		{#snippet children({ props })}
			<Label>Email</Label>
			<input type="email" {...props} bind:value={$formData.email} />
		{/snippet}
	</Control>
	{#snippet description()}We'll email you about your account.{/snippet}
</Field>
```

The `props` object reacts to field state. When validation produces errors, `aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby` and `data-fs-error` appear on the input automatically.

## The props object

| Attribute | Value |
| --------- | ----- |
| `name` | The field's path, used for form submission. |
| `id` | The control ID, used for label association. |
| `aria-describedby` | Space-separated IDs of the description and error containers; present only when description or validation exists. |
| `aria-invalid` | `"true"` when the field has errors, otherwise absent. |
| `aria-required` | `"true"` when the field's constraints mark it required, otherwise absent. |
| `data-fs-error` | Present when a validation error exists on the field. |
| `data-fs-control` | Always present; a styling hook. |

## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| ---- | ---- | ------- | ----------- |
| `id` | `string` | generated | The control's ID. Generated with Svelte's `$props.id()` when omitted, so it is stable between server rendering and hydration. |
| `children` | `Snippet<[{ props: ControlAttrs }]>` | — | Receives the spreadable `props` object described above. |

## Behavior notes

- **Requires a field scope.** `Control` reads context from an enclosing [Field](/docs/components/field), [Fieldset](/docs/components/fieldset) or [ElementField](/docs/components/element-field); outside one it throws.
- **Exactly one control per snippet.** Spread `props` onto the single element the label should point at. If you render several inputs, only one can carry the association.
- **Label pairing.** A [Label](/docs/components/label) rendered inside the same `Control` automatically gets `for` set to the resolved control ID — including an `id` you supplied yourself, which becomes part of the first server-rendered markup.
- **Style with data attributes.** `data-fs-control` and `data-fs-error` are stable selectors; see [Accessibility](/docs/guides/accessibility) for what Formsnap wires versus what stays your responsibility.

## When to use the hooks instead

Use `useFormControl` inside a custom control component to get the same `id`, `labelProps` and `props` without rendering the `Control` wrapper — for example when a third-party input library needs the attributes passed as props rather than spread onto a DOM element. It requires an enclosing `Control`. See [Custom controls](/docs/recipes/custom-controls).

## See also

- [Field](/docs/components/field) — the context `Control` reads from.
- [Label](/docs/components/label) — the label side of the association.
- [FieldErrors](/docs/components/field-errors) — the error container that `aria-describedby` points at.
